cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Antibiotic_Resistance_Models: MRSA endocarditis PK/PD simulation code"
abstract: >-
  Dual-compartment pharmacokinetic/pharmacodynamic model of MRSA endocarditis
  seeded from a bone reservoir, with Monte Carlo virtual-patient cohorts and
  Brent's-method transition points for linezolid EC50, linezolid Emax, and
  immune clearance.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Kammer
    given-names: Jacob W.
    affiliation: "Department of Mathematics and Statistical Science, University of Idaho"
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"
  - family-names: Udekwu
    given-names: Klas
    affiliation: "Department of Biological Science, University of Idaho"
  - family-names: Hernandez-Vargas
    given-names: Esteban A.
    affiliation: "Department of Mathematics and Statistical Science, University of Idaho"
repository-code: "https://github.com/jacobkammer/Antibiotic_Resistance_Models"
license: MIT
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-11-24"
# After Zenodo archives the GitHub release, add its version DOI:
# doi: "10.5281/zenodo.XXXXXXX"
keywords:
  - MRSA
  - infective endocarditis
  - osteomyelitis
  - pharmacokinetics
  - pharmacodynamics
  - linezolid
  - vancomycin
  - Monte Carlo simulation
